com/users/xglover410/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xglover410/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xglover410/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xglover410","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FC-OSP-6/trust-center/commits/4e10264997974faed8bd56a7be26693538eda3d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-24T17:54:53Z","email":"xglover410@gmail.com","name":"xglover410"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-24T17:54:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Completed Cache adapter refactor (#84)\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(runtime): switch root scripts to Bun-first commands and freeze the repo runtime entry contract\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(runtime): add Bun lockfile so local and CI installs use a reproducible dependency contract\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(runtime): retain npm lockfile temporarily while Bun becomes the authoritative package manager\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(stencil): name the workspace and replace npm pretest usage for consistent Bun execution\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(e2e): point root Playwright webServer orchestration at the Bun-first dev command\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): align Stencil Playwright startup command with the Bun-first workspace contract\n\n* part of MIL-338: ci(runtime): migrate install format test and build workflow steps to Bun-first commands\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(repo): ignore generated build and Playwright artifacts to keep verification output non-regressive\n\n* part of MIL-338: fix(fallback): treat Supabase tenant startup auth failures as valid seed fallback conditions\n\n* part of MIL-338: feat(api): return seed-backed mock data when GraphQL requests fail during runtime outages\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(api): cover controls faqs and overview fallback behavior during GraphQL outage scenarios\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(e2e): add healthy route smoke and outage fallback coverage for Overview Controls and FAQs\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): mark dormant control card specs skipped so the Bun test runner stays executable\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): add skipped placeholder coverage for dormant expansion card spec parity\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): add skipped placeholder coverage for dormant faq card spec parity\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): add skipped placeholder coverage for dormant subnav card spec parity\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(runtime): update README commands and lockfile guidance for the Bun-first developer workflow\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(config): document Bun-first script surface and CI runtime behavior\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(testing): describe new browser smoke and outage fallback coverage under Bun\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(testing): update Playwright runtime comment to reference the Bun-first dev command\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(db): update explain helper usage comment to reference bun run db:explain\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(runtime): remove npm lockfile now that Bun is the authoritative runtime contract\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(repo): stop tracking generated Playwright report artifacts in the git tree\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(stencil): stop tracking generated shared type shim output in the repo\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(stencil): stop tracking generated shared type shim sourcemaps in the repo\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(repo): stop tracking generated Playwright last-run state in the git tree\n\n* part of MIL-338: chore(repo): ignore regenerated Stencil shared type shim artifacts to keep the git tree clean\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(testing): replace stale empty-e2e note with current browser smoke and fallback coverage\n\n* part of MIL-338: docs(testing): document Stencil-local specs and root component bridge coverage ownership\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): replace control card placeholder spec with real grouped rendering and error coverage\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): add real expansion card coverage for static and controls rendering states\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): replace faq card placeholder spec with grouped and single-mode assertions\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(stencil): replace subnav placeholder spec with parsing empty and jump event coverage\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(e2e): make healthy controls smoke deterministic alongside outage fallback browser coverage\n\n* part of MIL-338: test(components): add root bridge coverage for shared React-to-Stencil wrapper markup\n\n* part of MIL-345: chore(docker): ignore local env and generated build artifacts so Docker builds use a clean reproducible context\n\n* part of MIL-345: chore(compose): freeze the root service map ports and inactive-redis runtime contract for the first Docker lane\n\n* part of MIL-346: chore(runtime): add a Bun-native server start script so the API can boot in containers without a watch loop\n\n* part of MIL-346: feat(api): add a Bun-first image recipe that installs the workspace and starts the real server process\n\n* part of MIL-346: chore(compose): add the API health check and runtime env needed for Docker host verification\n\n* part of MIL-347: feat(vite): allow container-safe host binding while preserving the existing proxy and /trust-center base path\n\n* part of MIL-347: feat(frontend): add a Bun-first image recipe that generates Stencil artifacts before starting Vite\n\n* part of MIL-347: chore(compose): wire the frontend service to the api hostname and explicit Vite container host binding\n\n* part of MIL-348: chore(runtime): switch Bun-executed DB scripts to native Bun commands so container verification can run migrations and seeding\n\n* part of MIL-348: feat(compose): add healthy postgres and redis services plus health-gated startup ordering for full-stack boot\n\n* part of MIL-348: feat(runtime): rename the stable server entrypoint and add docker dev helper scripts for local and remote stack boot\n\n* part of MIL-348: chore(api): point the Docker API image at the renamed stable Bun server runtime script\n\n* part of MIL-348: feat(compose): allow an opt-in remote database override while keeping local Postgres as the default Docker path\n\n* part of MIL-348: docs(config): document the opt-in Docker remote database override and its safety caveats\n\n* part of MIL-348: fix(runtime): trap docker dev exits so ctrl+c tears down compose services and frees published ports\n\n* part of MIL-348: chore(runtime): separate docker build output from focused api and frontend dev logs while preserving ctrl+c cleanup\n\n* part of MIL-348: docs(readme): document the Docker dev workflow endpoints and remote database override\n\n* Testing agentic coding\n\n* chore(git): untrack .claude/ and CLAUDE.md — local-only agentic tooling\n\n* Testing agentic coding\n\n* feat(scripts): reserve open local ports before starting concurrent development processes safely\n\n* build(scripts): coordinate local service startup so development commands avoid occupied ports reliably\n\n* feat(vite): choose an open local frontend port and keep proxy targets aligned\n\n* test(playwright): follow the selected local frontend port when starting end to end runs\n\n* test(tooling): verify local launcher shares open ports and respects manual overrides\n\n* test(vite): confirm local port coordination works across config and development scripts\n\n* chore(config): document the frontend development port so local runs can coordinate services\n\n* docs(config): describe coordinated local port allocation across server client and test tooling\n\n* docs(readme): explain shared local port selection and how development URLs now change\n\n* finished cache adapter refactor\n\n* feat(chatbot-rail): styling complete (#83)\n\nCo-authored-by: Annie Tadvick <annie.tadvick@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elijah Morris <morrisxelijah@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Annie Tadvick <annie.tadvick@gmail.com>\nCo-au