resource readyWhen condition to check for \"Ready\" status instead of \"SystemComponentsHealthy\" and add AllTrue readiness policy to ensure proper resource state validation in KRO configuration.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat(flux): add OCM component dependency and refactor GraphQL gateway configuration\n\n- Add basic-ocm dependency to flux kustomization\n- Add ocmComponentRef parameter to GraphQL gateway resource definition\n- Remove embedded OCM repository and component resources in favor of external dependency\n- Fix indentation inconsistencies in YAML configurations\n- Simplify resource definitions by referencing external OCM components\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: update ocmComponentRef default name in GraphQL gateway RGD\n\nChange default ocmComponentRef name from ''kubernetes-graphql-gateway'' to ''platform-mesh'' in the GraphQL gateway resource definition to align with new component naming conventions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add OCM component reference to GraphQL gateway configuration\n\nAdd ocmComponentRef field with platform-mesh component name to the basic GraphQL gateway manifest to enable OCM integration and component tracking.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add referencePath to GraphQL gateway resource definition\n\nAdd referencePath configuration with kubernetes-graphql-gateway name to chart and image resource references in the KRO basic example manifest to properly specify resource paths within the OCM component.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add examples documentation and Flux dependency ordering\n\n- Add comprehensive examples section to README documenting the demo manifests structure\n- Configure Flux Kustomization dependencies: basic-app depends on basic-shoot, basic-shoot depends on basic-kro\n- Establish proper deployment order for platform components (KRO → Shoot → App → GraphQL Gateway)\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>","tree":{"sha":"68d9868758ce3d75be4c7f0ac7ce21e0748f1e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmcp-project/local-event-showcase/git/trees/68d9868758ce3d75be4c7f0ac7ce21e0748f1e66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmcp-project/local-event-showcase/git/commits/767c6eb6fb8aeaf43e7128a2a41f7900a858472e","verification":{"payload":"tree 68d9868758ce3d75be4c7f0ac7ce21e0748f1e66\nparent 88b47ae51888026c52e6856fca09b896fc810eb7\nauthor Aaron Schweig <42006873+aaronschweig@users.noreply.github.com> 1774258122 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774258122 +0100\n\nfeat: use ocm to deploy kgg (#16)\n\n* feat: use ocm to deploy kgg\n\n* feat: update shoot readiness condition and add readiness policy\n\nUpdate shoot resource readyWhen condition to check for \"Ready\" status instead of \"SystemComponentsHealthy\" and add AllTrue readiness policy to ensure proper resource state validation in KRO configuration.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat(flux): add OCM component dependency and refactor GraphQL gateway configuration\n\n- Add basic-ocm dependency to flux kustomization\n- Add ocmComponentRef parameter to GraphQL gateway resource definition\n- Remove embedded OCM repository and component resources in favor of external dependency\n- Fix indentation inconsistencies in YAML configurations\n- Simplify resource definitions by referencing external OCM components\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: update ocmComponentRef default name in GraphQL gateway RGD\n\nChange default ocmComponentRef name from ''kubernetes-graphql-gateway'' to ''platform-mesh'' in the GraphQL gateway resource definition to align with new component naming conventions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add OCM component reference to GraphQL gateway configuration\n\nAdd ocmComponentRef field with platform-mesh component name to the basic GraphQL gateway manifest to enable OCM integration and component tracking.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add referencePath to GraphQL gateway resource definition\n\nAdd referencePath configuration with kubernetes-graphql-gateway name to chart and image resource references in the KRO basic example manifest to properly specify resource paths within the OCM component.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n* feat: add examples documentation and Flux dependency ordering\n\n- Add comprehensive examples section to README documenting the demo manifests structure\n- Configure Flux Kustomization dependencies: basic-app depends on basic-shoot, basic-shoot depends on basic-kro\n- Establish proper deployment order for platform components (KRO → Shoot → App → GraphQL Gateway)\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.e